	(text "# POWER SUPPLY SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (REGULATOR BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet - COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe power supply subsystem utilizes two independent TPS63020DSJR buck-boost converters to separate the digital core from sensitive analog measurement blocks.\nDual converters prevent high-frequency digital switching noise and transient load ripples from degrading precision sensor readings and ADC reference baselines.\n\n1. DIGITAL POWER RAIL SETUP (+3.3V / +3.3VD)\nConverter IC: U2 (TPS63020DSJR high-efficiency buck-boost converter).\nFunction: Regulates variable VDD input (USB 5V or LiPo battery 3.0V-4.2V) to a stable +3.3V digital supply rail.\nInput Decoupling: C2 (10µF), C3 (10µF), and C4 (100nF) MLCC ceramic capacitors placed close to pins VIN_10, VIN_11, and VINA.\nFeedback Network: Voltage divider using R6 (1MΩ) and R7 (180kΩ) tied to pin 3 (FB) sets the output voltage regulation to exact +3.3V (VFB = 0.5V, VOUT = 0.5V * (1 + 1M/180k) = 3.278V ~ 3.3V).\nOutput Filtering: Main digital output is filtered by C5 (47µF) bulk ceramic capacitor.\nPower Good Monitor: Pin 14 (PG) pulled up to VOUT through R5 (100kΩ).\nPower Inductor: L1 (1.5µH) connected across switching terminals L1 (pins 8, 9) and L2 (pins 6, 7).\nControl Pins: EN (pin 12) tied to VDD and PS/SYNC (pin 13) grounded for continuous forced PWM active-mode operation.\n\n2. CLEAN ANALOG POWER RAIL SETUP (+3.3VA)\nConverter IC: U3 (TPS63020DSJR high-efficiency buck-boost converter).\nFunction: Regulates variable VDD input into an isolated, ultra-clean +3.3VA supply rail for the analog front-end (OPA2320S, INA333, ADS1115 ADCs).\nInput Decoupling: C6 (10µF), C7 (10µF), and C8 (100nF) ceramic capacitors connected across VIN_10, VIN_11, and VINA.\nFeedback Network: Voltage divider using R9 (1MΩ) and R10 (180kΩ) tied to pin 3 (FB) sets the analog output rail regulation to +3.3VA.\nOutput Filtering: Low-pass output filtering provided by C9 (47µF) bulk ceramic capacitor.\nPower Good Monitor: Pin 14 (PG) pulled up to VOUT through R8 (100kΩ).\nPower Inductor: L2 (1.5µH) connected across switching terminals L1 (pins 8, 9) and L2 (pins 6, 7).\nControl Pins: EN (pin 12) tied to VDD and PS/SYNC (pin 13) grounded for low-noise continuous mode operation.\n\n3. GROUND PLANE & RULE VERIFICATION SETUP\nCommon System Ground (GND): Solid common ground return plane utilized across all 4 layers under Revision 3.3 to eliminate loop antennas and return-path discontinuities.\nPWR_FLAG: Tied directly to the power rails and GND nets on both U2 and U3 output domains for automated KiCad Electrical Rules Check (ERC) power-driver verification."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.208 47.244 0)
